<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The trip-tracking notification's small icon — Odo's own gauge mark, the same two arcs
    as the launcher's `ic_launcher_foreground`, so the status bar shows the app's mark
    rather than a glyph that only exists here.

    Both arcs are drawn white because a notification's small icon is a silhouette: Android
    keeps only the alpha channel and re-tints every pixel with the notification's accent
    colour, so the launcher's grey-over-black pair would read as one shape regardless.
    Drawing both anyway keeps the union — the slightly longer outer sweep is what makes the
    mark read as Odo's gauge and not a plain ring.

    Scaled up from the launcher's 0.77: the adaptive-icon safe zone it was sized for does
    not apply to a 24dp status-bar glyph, which should fill its box instead.

    A byte-for-byte twin of `:core:platform`'s drawable of the same name. The two modules
    share no Android library between them, so there is nowhere to put one copy without
    inventing a dependency edge for an icon. Change one, change the other.
-->
